# commit-guard exemptions. One fnmatch pattern per line.
# `entropy:` scopes a line to the entropy tier only — block-tier rules
# (env files, private keys, credential literals) still apply everywhere.

# A deliberately long, unbroken filename fixture. The test it feeds asserts
# that such a name wraps instead of widening the mobile layout, so it cannot
# be shortened. Long + unbroken is exactly what the entropy heuristic flags.
entropy:src/__tests__/components/evidence-manager.test.tsx

# A module path in a `vi.mock` call, long enough to read as a random token.
entropy:src/__tests__/app/route-planner-ui.test.tsx

# .env.local.example documents the variables a local checkout needs. It is an
# example file, but its name misses the scanner's exempt suffixes, which come
# after ".env", not after ".env.local". Its S3 values are the bundled MinIO
# container's own dev credentials (farecheck_dev / farecheck_dev_secret against
# 127.0.0.1:9000), already in compose.dev.yml and useless off localhost.
# Content rules still apply: a real credential added here is still blocked.
env-file:.env.local.example

# Same file, entropy tier: the `your_google_..._here` style placeholders read as
# high-entropy strings. Real key formats and PEM blocks still block here.
entropy:.env.local.example
